-- title:
--   Weighted local Bézout bound from codimension
-- statement:
--   The weighted local Bézout step: for an ideal generated by polynomials of weighted degree at most positive `H`, its finite local component length at a minimal prime is bounded by `2 * H ^ A.card` after multiplication by the selected coordinate weights, provided `A.card` equals the prime height. A concrete route is to compare the local quotient length with that of a parameter slice and apply weighted Bézout to the slice, carrying the weight allowances through the estimate. The zero-height case has empty `A` and uses the empty product convention.

import Definitions.Def_OAI_PiExponent_LogarithmicNormalBases
import Definitions.Def_OAI_PiExponent_ComponentLocalLength
